<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47883" body-key="">*<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάομαι</span></b> , a form needlessly
		invented to expl. the foll. 
			Dor.
		 forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾱέομαι</span> (q.v.), in
		which <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾱ-</span> is 
			contr.
		 fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾱε</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ο</span>)- and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾱη-</span>:
			1pl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sophr.
					85
				</span></i>
			: 2pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾶσθε</span> (Megar.) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				770
			</span></i>; imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάεο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>APl.</u>
					4.306
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.354
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nossis</span>); part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάμενος, ταὶ θάμεναι τὰ
			Ἴσθμια</span>, title of mime by Sophron, Arg.<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θασεῖσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Cer.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			: fut.part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θασόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					15.23
				</span></i>
			: aor. imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾶσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					114
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.149
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.12
			</span></i>; inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.72
				</span></i>
			; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θασάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
					1.118
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			 only in part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάοντα: διδάσκοντα, θεωροῦντα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, and 
				Lacon.
			
			1pl.
			impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσᾱμεν</span> (i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθᾱμεν</span>),= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθεωροῦμεν</span>, Id.</div>
